From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: SFP files - mdio-i2c shim and missing prototypes

sfp_phy.c dereferences the QSDK-only struct qcom_mdio_i2c_data, which
the vendor kernel defines in include/linux/mdio/mdio-i2c.h when its
mdio-i2c driver is present (vendor patches 0643/0934).  Mainline 6.12
has no such struct:

  src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c:66:44: error: invalid use of undefined type
    'struct qcom_mdio_i2c_data'

Provide a compile-only definition guarded by MIDO_I2C_QCOM, the macro
the vendor header defines.  The code path using it (->i2c on an mii_bus
whose id contains "i2c") is only reachable with that vendor driver, and
ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts has no mdio-i2c node, so this is inert on target.

Classification: must-shim (vendor kernel ABI, no mainline equivalent;
compile-only until the mdio-i2c driver is ported).

Remaining missing prototypes: sfp_phy_part_number_check(),
sfp_phy_usxgmii_check() and sfp_phy_present_status_check() are used only
within sfp_phy.c, so make them static.  adpt_sfp.c never includes
adpt_sfp.h (which declares adpt_sfp_init()) and its 16 other sfp ops are
referenced only from adpt_sfp_init(), so include the header and give
them internal linkage.

